<title>MALAYSIA: MAS says settles pilots' wage dispute.</title>
<headline>MAS says settles pilots' wage dispute.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>National carrier Malaysian Airline System Bhd (MAS) said on Wednesday it settled a long-standing wage dispute with its pilots' association.</p>
<p>MAS chairman Tajudin Ramli said on Malaysia's private channel TV3 that the agreement with Malaysia Airlines Pilots Association (MAPA) will give pilots a salary increase higher than what they were asking. He gave no further details.</p>
<p>Tajudin is in Seattle to witness the roll-out of MAS's first Boeing B777 aircraft. The airline is buying 10 777-200 planes, five 777-300s and 10 747-400s costing 10 billion ringgit from Boeing.</p>
</text>
